Assembler Version 07
====================
Assembled by: version 06 (both instgen and asm)

Features Supported by This Assembler
-------------------------------------
Same non-standard mnemonic syntax as version 06, with improved error handling,
error diagnostics with line numbers, stderr output, and PC management:

Syntax:
- Non-standard (custom) mnemonic syntax: LDA#, LDAZ, STAZ, etc.
- DATA pseudo-instruction for raw byte emission
- Hex constants: $xx (1 byte) or $xxxx (2 bytes)
- Quoted strings with \n escape
- Label definitions with PC value or explicit assignment
- PC setting via: * = $xxxx (with zero-fill between old and new PC on pass 2)
- Low byte (<) and high byte (>) operators on labels
- Relative branch (~label) syntax (still supported but also auto-detected via flags)
- Labels as 2-byte operands
- Comments with semicolons
- Two-pass assembly
- Flag-based operand type detection (INST_RELATIVE, INST_BYTE, INST_PSUEDO)
- Zero page addressing uses plain hex values without the < prefix (e.g., STAZ $07
  rather than STAZ <$07)

Instruction set: same as version 06

Error handling (expanded):
- Label not found (error 1)
- Duplicate label (error 2)
- Opcode not found (error 3)
- Expected hex value (error 4)
- Branch out of range (error 5)
- Value out of range (error 6)
- Invalid hex (error 7)
- PC value expected (error 8)
- Closing quote not found (error 9)
- Cannot move PC backwards (error A)

New in this version (relative to version 06):
- Interrupt handler for formatted error output: errors displayed via BRK
  interrupt with error code and inline message string
- Stderr output via write_d ($F00C): error messages written to stderr
- Decimal number formatting (to_decimal): line numbers in error messages
  displayed in decimal
- Line number tracking: CURLINEL/CURLINEH count input lines, included in
  error messages (format: "Error N at line M: message")
- Exit vector at $FFFC/$FFFE for interrupt/reset handling
- Hex input validation: detects and reports invalid hex characters (error 7)
- Value out of range checking for single-byte operands (error 6)
- PC value expected error when * used without = assignment (error 8)
- Closing quote not found error with newline detection (error 9)
- Cannot move PC backwards error (error A)
- Zero-fill between old and new PC positions on pass 2 (update_pc)
- STARTED flag to track whether output has begun
- Zero page addresses used without < prefix (e.g., STAZ MEMPL instead of
  STAZ <MEMPL), meaning the assembler uses raw zero-page addresses
- read_token now checks for end-of-token before storing (reordered loop)

